uild-version calendar (CSV) so the agent pins the regression to the exact build that shipped the nerf — no ETL.<br>**USP:** It speaks *game-design*, not analytics — output is "Boss at Level 5 post-patch v2.3.1 causes a 3x death-quit loop, D7 -11%; revert the HP buff." The `sequenceMatch` rage-quit fingerprint + chDB patch-version join is a non-obvious, designer-native use of ClickHouse.<br>**Demoability:** Prompt "why did D7 drop after last week's patch?" It runs pre/post retention, walks the progression funnel to the failing level live, surfaces the death-loop sequence, joins the patch calendar to name the build, and prints a tuning recommendation.<br><br>### 5. HookRadar — *music streaming A&R*<br>**One-liner:** An autonomous A&R scout that mines skip-and-replay behavior across billions of stream events to flag breakout tracks and diagnose why a release is dying in the first 30 seconds.<br>**M&E problem:** Record labels and streaming editorial/A&R teams need to spot a breaking track *before* it peaks and understand skip behavior to fix release strategy. The signal — where listeners skip, replay, or save — lives in massive event logs that A&R people can't query, so they rely on lagging chart data and gut feel.<br>**How the agent works:** Gemini introspects the stream-event schema, then reasons about "hit potential vs skip risk" and drills: track → skip-timestamp distribution → the exact second listeners bail → replay/save velocity by region. It autonomously segments by playlist context and cohort. Agent Builder runs a breakout-detector sub-agent, a skip-forensics SQL sub-agent, and an A&R-brief writer in a loop that ranks tracks by momentum.<br>**Partner integration (the core):** `run_query` using `sequenceMatch('(?1)(?2)')` over `(play_start, skip_before_30s)` to compute the "hook fail" rate, `quantile(0.5)(skip_second)` to pinpoint the exact drop-off moment in the track, `retention()` for day-over-day re-listen (the truest hit signal), `uniqExact(listener_id)` for reach, and `topK(25)(track_id)` by save-velocity. `run_chdb_select_query` joins internal stream momentum against *external* social/Shazam/chart CSVs (zero ETL) to separate organic breakouts from paid-push noise and confirm cross-platform lift.<br>**USP:** Turns raw stream telemetry into A&R decisions with a per-second skip diagnosis ("83% skip at 0:22 — the intro is too long") — a musically actionable insight, not a stream count. The replay-`retention` + external-chart chDB join distinguishes real momentum from manufactured hype, which is the A&R holy grail.<br>**Demoability:** Prompt "find this week's breakout and tell me what's killing the new single." It ranks tracks by save-velocity, drills the single's skip curve to the 0:22 drop-off, joins external chart data to confirm organic lift on the breakout, and outputs a one-page A&R brief.<br><br>---<br><br>## 🔴 Replit Track<br><br>*Built with **Replit Agent** AND deployed on a live `replit.app`/`replit.dev` URL. Surface: Replit Agent (prompt-to-app scaffolding + programmatic Agent API), Replit Deployments (instant hosting + live URL), Replit DB (key-value live state), Replit Auth, Object Storage, scheduled/always-on backends. The live URL is the demo hook.*<br><br>> **Note:** These assume a *programmatic* Replit Agent API. If programmatic invocation isn't currently available, each idea still works by having you drive Replit Agent in-IDE — the load-bearing requirement is the live Replit deployment. Confirm the current Agent API surface against Replit's docs before building.<br><br>### 1. PremiereForge — *film marketing / promo distribution*<br>**One-liner:** An agent that takes a film's raw assets and autonomously builds, deploys, and self-repairs a live interactive promo microsite on its own replit.app URL.<br>**M&E problem:** Studio and indie marketing teams burn days and agency money spinning up bespoke promo sites per title; most never ship interactive fan features because there's no dev bandwidth before the re